# agent-tty and its Claude Code skill: desktop + container only. The npm
# package itself is cross-platform (no os/cpu restriction, engines node
# >=24 <27, and `nix: nodejs_24` is in packages.yaml for every nix host) — this
# gate is not about platform support, it is about not pulling a node toolchain
# onto headless servers, which have no TUI to drive. Ignore the script and the
# skill together so a server never gets a skill for a binary it lacks.
.chezmoiscripts/unix/75-install-npm-packages.sh
.claude/skills/agent-tty
{{ end }}

{{ if not (lookPath "codex") }}
# codex's config.toml is codex-owned state; a modify_ script asserts three keys
# in it (see dot_codex/) rather than managing the file. Skip where codex isn't
# installed so we don't create a config for a program that isn't there. Same
# first-apply caveat as herdr below: codex comes from the nix profile that
# before_03 builds, so it isn't resolvable until the next run on a fresh host.
.codex/config.toml
{{ end }}

{{ if not (lookPath "herdr") }}
# herdr Claude Code skill: generated by running `herdr --skill`, so it can only
# render where herdr is on PATH — every nix host, but not Windows. Also skipped
# on the first apply of a fresh host: the nix profile is created by before_03,
# after chezmoi's own PATH is fixed, so herdr isn't resolvable until the next
# run. Skipping beats failing the whole apply on a missing binary.
.claude/skills/herdr
{{ end }}

